  "authors": [],
  "body": {
    "comment": "本Info ActionにYESと投票します。\nstakePoolTargetNum（k）は2020年に150から500へ引き上げられて以降、約6年間変更されていません。今回500から1000へ引き上げれば、報酬上の飽和点は約75M ADAから約37.5M ADAへ下がり、大規模Poolに集中したStakeの再流動化を促します。\n近年はSPOを立ち上げる環境は改善した一方、Nodeの資源要求や冗長化、監視、セキュリティ、ガバナンス対応など安定運営の負担は増えています。また、Reserve由来のStaking Rewardは長期的に減少する構造にあり、新規・小規模SPOがDelegationを獲得する重要性は高まっています。\nk=1000だけで分散化が保証されるわけではありませんが、Stakeの再流動化を促すことはCardanoの分散化を進める合理的な措置だと考えます。\n\n---\n\nI vote YES on this Info Action.\n\nstakePoolTargetNum (k) was increased from 150 to 500 in 2020 and has remained unchanged for about six years. Raising it from 500 to 1000 would lower the reward saturation point from about 75M ADA to 37.5M ADA, encouraging stake concentrated in larger pools to move again.\n\nWhile it has become easier to start an SPO, the burden of stable operation has increased due to higher node resource requirements, redundancy, monitoring, security, and governance responsibilities. At the same time, staking rewards from the reserve are designed to decline over the long term, making access to delegation increasingly important for new and smaller SPOs.\n\nk=1000 alone will not guarantee decentralization, but encouraging stake redistribution is a reasonable step toward improving Cardano’s decentralization."
  },
  "hashAlgorithm": "blake2b-256"
}